\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Those are good questions. To answer them, we look to the oracle's structure. \
Ezekiel introduces the metaphor of the people as dross in verse 18. Then, he makes a claim in verse 19 - because they are dross, they will be gathered in Jerusalem. \
But then, this is interpreted in verse 20 to 22. And that interpretation does not focus on the disappointing nature of the materials. No - it talks about silver, the outcome of the process, and about the LORD's wrath, the means of the process. That is, heat produces silver. Verse 19 calls the people dross of silver. But verse 22 says that as silver is melted in a furnace, so they will be melted, connecting this with the recognition formula.
