\cf2 Related to silver production even as impurities is a better summary than I had myself. In and of themselves, they are dross. And yet, silver is produced. When verse 22 says that they will know the LORD is the LORD, it says this will come about by their recognition that the LORD has poured out his fury on them. Other oracles explore the implications, but this oracle stops at that point. The rhetoric is a response to an incorrect self view by the people. They are dross, whether or not they want to acknowledge that fact - the LORD's assessment is the objectively correct one. But the fury of the LORD will be beyond their ability not to acknowledge. That this fury will be the heat that melts and refines is central to the metaphor.
