\cf2 Optimizing for self-interest, forgetting that human life has sanctity before God, and treating the vulnerable as resources to exploit have hardly ended since Ezekiel's time, though the Bible's influence may have in some times and places held back some forms of such.\
I am very cautious about generalizing God's judgement on Jerusalem. But generalizing the immorality of bloodshed, broadly understood, does seem appropriate. As does generalizing the warning against patterns which enable such bloodshed.
