\b0\fs24 \cf2 You will study Ezekiel thinking you understand bloodshed. You don't. Neither did I.\
Ezekiel 22 forced me to see that bloodshed encompasses far more than direct violence. When princes used power 
\f2 \uc0\u1488 \u1460 \u1497 \u1513 \u1473 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1460 \u1494 \u1456 \u1512 \u1465 \u1506 \u1493 \u1465 
\f1  - "each according to his arm/strength" - 
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1456 \u1502 \u1463 \u1506 \u1463 \u1503 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1513 \u1456 \u1473 \u1508 \u1464 \u1498 \u1456 \u1470 \u1491 \u1464 \u1468 \u1501 
\f1  - "for the purpose of shedding blood" (v. 6), the subsequent evidence (vv. 7-12) spans economic exploitation, oppression of the vulnerable, sexual violations, and ritual negligence. All of these serve bloodshed because they express contempt for human life.\
The text doesn't present separate categories where some violations are violent and others merely social or economic. It presents a unified pattern: treating human life as expendable for other goals. Making light of parents (v. 7a). Oppressing sojourner, orphan, widow (v. 7b). Taking bribes and interest (v. 12a). These are bloodshed because they demonstrate predatory use of power against those without it.\
Most critically: verse 12 explains 
\f2 \uc0\u1493 \u1456 \u1488 \u1465 \u1514 \u1460 \u1497 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1513 \u1464 \u1473 \u1499 \u1463 \u1495 \u1463 \u1514 \u1456 \u1468 
\f1  - "and Me you have forgotten." This isn't theological ignorance but practical optimization that left out the primary constraint. They knew Torah. They knew covenant obligations. But they optimized for wealth, power, security, efficiency - forgetting that human life has sanctity before God that cannot be negotiated away.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa240\partightenfactor0

\b \cf2 The mechanism matters:
\b0  Genesis 4 and Leviticus 18 show guilt and defilement are objective realities, not just divine accounting. Abel's blood cries out (Gen 4:10). The land becomes defiled and vomits out inhabitants (Lev 18:25,28). Ezekiel 22:3-4 uses infinitives of result: bloodshed and idolatry don't just deserve punishment - they bring the appointed time, accumulate defilement that makes continued habitation impossible. This is why verse 15's scattering serves to consume defilement from Jerusalem - removing the source of pollution.\

