Watch for your own deflection patterns. I explained these oracles while treating them as ancient content rather than present reality. I analyzed the audience's blindness while remaining blind myself. I used sophisticated language to maintain observer distance. The backwards assessment method exposed this: looking at what I said versus what I avoided, recognizing aversion versus mere distraction, noticing performative sophistication that obscures rather than illuminates.\
The text itself falsifies compartmentalization. There are no neutral domains where divine sovereignty doesn't apply, no spheres where contempt for life becomes acceptable through normalization. When you encounter violence, economic exploitation, or systems treating humans as expendable throughout Ezekiel, remember: this is all bloodshed because it expresses the same predatory pattern the princes demonstrated - using power to prey on the vulnerable while forgetting God.\
